Zeile 0: 0.05-1.95  Why the FBI never found this man.
Zeile 1: 2.05-6.44  In 1971, a quiet man in a suit boarded a flight to Seattle.
Zeile 2: 6.54-9.37  He handed the flight attendant a note. He had a bomb.
Zeile 3: 9.47-12.52  He wanted two hundred thousand dollars, and four parachutes.
Zeile 4: 12.62-15.43  In Seattle, he swapped the passengers for the money.
Zeile 5: 15.53-18.96  Then, at night, in a storm, he jumped out of the back of the plane.
Zeile 6: 19.06-23.69  Nine years later, a boy found five thousand eight hundred dollars of it by a river.
Zeile 7: 23.79-26.33  The rest was never found. And neither was he.
Zeile 8: 26.43-28.31  Would you have jumped?
